      "side": 1,
      "message": "Same bound relaxation on the encode side. The 64-bit branch added below does\n\n    memcpy(\u0026val, present_reading, sizeof(val));\n\nwhich reads eight bytes from a const uint8_t * supplied by the caller. encode_get_sensor_reading_resp() is also ABI_STABLE, so an existing caller passing the address of a 32-bit value would now be read out of bounds when sensor_data_size says uint64.\n\nSeparately, swapping PLDM_EFFECTER_DATA_SIZE_* for PLDM_SENSOR_DATA_SIZE_* in this function is a good fix on its own - the two enumerations happen to agree today but nothing requires them to.",
      "revId": "817cfb8f785c55f10f7c21d3876ef3a5e28ef768",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
